}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3 rows x (3*N) cols, where N = 3 panels [observed, solver supports any N >= 1]
  colors_input: BLACK (background) and GREY (symbol pixels) only
  panels:
    size: 3x3, tiled left-to-right with no gaps
    content: each panel is a binary grey/black glyph from a fixed codebook of 5 symbols
    # codebook (1=GREY, 0=BLACK):
    #   GREEN  = [[1,1,1],[1,0,1],[1,1,1]]  (hollow square, 8 grey)
    #   YELLOW = [[0,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,0]]  (center dot, 1 grey)
    #   MAROON = [[0,0,1],[0,1,0],[1,0,0]]  (anti-diagonal, 3 grey)
    #   BLUE   = [[0,0,0],[0,0,0],[1,1,1]]  (bottom row, 3 grey)
    #   PINK   = [[1,1,1],[0,0,0],[0,0,0]]  (top row, 3 grey)
    no_repeats: true -- each symbol appears at most once across panels [observed]
  transform:
    rule: replace each 3x3 panel with a solid 3x3 block of the codebook-decoded color
    output_colors: GREEN(3), YELLOW(4), MAROON(9), BLUE(1), PINK(6)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is trivially constructable)
  steps:
    1. Choose N = 3 [observed] panels (solver supports any N >= 1).
    2. Sample N distinct symbols from the 5-entry codebook without replacement.
    3. Arrange their order randomly (permutation).
    4. Build the 3 x (3*N) grid by placing each symbol's grey/black mask side-by-side.
```
